a number called 'cupboard rounded reading' is {'the dispatch note reading' add 0.5} as a number.
If 'cupboard rounded reading' is not 232641479 then, Print "ASSERT EXP-94: expected 232641479 got {'cupboard rounded reading'}", Exit 95. Print 'cupboard rounded reading'.

--- the same leaf, a seed with fraction at or above .50 (rounds up) ---
a float called 'notebook reading' is 7.31.
a number called 'the message slip rounded reading' is {'notebook reading' add 0.5} as a number.
If 'the message slip rounded reading' is not 7 then, Print "ASSERT EXP-94: expected 7 got {'the message slip rounded reading'}", Exit 95. Print 'the message slip rounded reading'.

--- the same leaf, the extreme-value cliff: whole part is i64::MAX, float64 cannot represent it exactly, the naive oracle diverges (documented candidate, see report) ---
